Patch: 018-apply-patch-off
Reason: with the built-ins off, code mode (code_mode_host) still listed Codex's own apply_patch as a nested tool of exec though it has no environment to run in, so every call failed "No usable execution environment is available" (15 dead calls in 7 of 29 benchmark runs). Codex 0.164 has no feature that removes it (apply_patch_freeform is removed); its model catalog's apply_patch_tool_type does. The harness reads the binary's own bundled catalog (codex debug models --bundled), sets that one field null on every model (withoutApplyPatch), uploads it to CODEX_HOME and names it in model_catalog_json, a key an app may not set. With the built-ins on, apply_patch stays.
Upstream: ours
Pins: Codex's bundled catalog without apply_patch: that one field null on every model, everything else as Codex ships it
Pins: the config names the catalog Codex reads (model_catalog_json) when given one, and an app may not set it
Pins: with the built-ins off, a code-mode model (luna, sol) is offered no apply_patch of Codex's own: exec lists none, and config.toml names the catalog that turns it off
